{"name":"Grey Blue","hex":"#77a1b5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey-blue","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray-blue: synonym of blue-gray."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray-blue: synonym of blue-gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey-blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue-gray","blocks":[{"text":"Blue-gray is a medium blue-gray color on the cool side of the color wheel. The name blue-gray was introduced by Crayola for a crayon color used from 1958 to 1990. The complementary color is #CC9966, a warm khaki or brown."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue-gray","wikidata":"Q4928721"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Ea